 "_doc": "Unit motion pass 2026-11-13 (production/qa/evidence/unit-motion/audit.md). Procedural pose on top of the sheet clips, whole art px only (art bible 8.10: no rotation, no non-integer scale, no half pixels). The frame is drawn as three bands from the same source rect: legs (never moves, feet pinned), torso (rows above waist_ratio of the body height) and head (rows above chest_ratio). lean = head band offset along screen x (the torso gets half, rounded down); squash = torso + head pushed DOWN (never up, so no gap opens). Fields: idle_speed = idle clip clock multiplier; breath_px / breath_sec / breath_duty = idle squash depth, period and the share of the period spent dipped; sway_px / sway_sec = slow idle head lean (weight shift); hover_px / hover_sec = whole-body bob, only for sprites drawn in the air (ghosts, wisps, bats, sprites; a creature whose feet touch the ground is never floaty: the feet stay on the cell); the shadow stays and narrows; slide_scale = multiplier on hit_feel.step_slide_sec for the drawn glide; hop_px = arc height of the glide; lean_px = head lean into a move; anticipate = share of the glide with the head leaning back first; land_squash_px / settle_sec = landing dip and follow-through after the glide; overshoot_px = whole-body overshoot past the target during the settle; windup_lean_px / windup_squash_px = coil while a windup / guard / howl clip runs (head away from the foe); hit_lean_px = head whiplash away from the blow while the recoil runs; release_sec = short dip when an action clip hands back to idle. units: id -> archetype name, or {archetype, ...overrides}. Unlisted ids use default. 2026-11-13 seam review (production/qa/evidence/unit-motion/review/README.md): Forest Witch and Goblin Warlock have sway_px 0, because a 1 px idle head lean slid their hair / staff / hat / stone pack against the hands and brim at the chest split; breathing, movement, windup and landing are unchanged.",
